2026-11-05T18:46:00.9936940Z [34m==>[0m [1mllvm[0m
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9937580Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_SYSTEM_DIR: /opt/homebrew/etc/clang
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9938010Z CLANG_CONFIG_FILE_USER_DIR:   ~/.config/clang
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9938210Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9938410Z LLD and LLDB are now provided in separate formulae:
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9938890Z   brew install lld
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9939210Z   brew install lldb
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9939410Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9939710Z Z3 solver support will be removed in LLVM 24 as it is unsupported upstream,
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9940480Z see https://github.com/llvm/llvm-project/pull/205370
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9940800Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9941230Z Using `clang`, `clang++`, etc., requires a CLT installation at `/Library/Developer/CommandLineTools`.
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9949000Z If you don't want to install the CLT, you can write appropriate configuration files pointing to your
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9949760Z SDK at ~/.config/clang.
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9949890Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9950110Z To use the bundled libunwind please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9962220Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9962570Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9962800Z To use the bundled libc++ please use the following LDFLAGS:
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9963610Z   LDFLAGS="-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/c++ -L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib/unwind -lunwind"
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9964310Z Features newer than system libc++ will require the following define to enable
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9964930Z (support for this may be removed in a future major LLVM release):
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9965460Z   CPPFLAGS="-D_LIBCPP_DISABLE_AVAILABILITY"
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9965750Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9966100Z NOTE: You probably want to use the libunwind and libc++ provided by macOS unless you know what you're doing.
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9966530Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9966680Z llvm is keg-only, which means it was not symlinked into /opt/homebrew,
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9967340Z because macOS already provides this software and installing another version in
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9967940Z parallel can cause all kinds of trouble.
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9968240Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9968520Z If you need to have llvm first in your PATH, run:
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9969120Z   printf '%s\n' export\ PATH\=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/bin:\$PATH >> /Users/runner/.bash_profile
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9969520Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9969690Z For compilers to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9970820Z   export LDFLAGS=-L/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/lib
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9971180Z   export CPPFLAGS=-I/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm/include
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9971420Z 
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9971560Z For cmake to find llvm you may need to set:
2026-11-05T18:46:00.9971980Z   export CMAKE_PREFIX_PATH=/opt/homebrew/opt/llvm
